To unite these two great families in marriage?

01:10:23.580 --> 01:10:29.350
My boy, I... I feel as though I have achieved at last something worthwhile.

01:10:30.090 --> 01:10:40.560
I just wanted you to know, my boy, that I'm happy.

01:12:30.000 --> 01:12:45.450
Nooo!

01:12:45.450 --> 01:12:46.340
Yes.

01:12:46.340 --> 01:12:47.340
But I am not funny.

01:12:47.340 --> 01:12:49.890
No?

01:12:49.890 --> 01:12:51.450
Who are you then?

01:12:51.450 --> 01:12:54.870
Why are you so anxious to know?

01:12:54.870 --> 01:12:58.920
Well, you're so exactly like a poor little girl I know who works in a restaurant.

01:12:58.920 --> 01:13:00.000
You think I...

01:13:00.120 --> 01:13:02.600
I'm this political girl who works in France?

01:13:02.600 --> 01:13:05.640
Oh, no, of course not.

01:13:05.640 --> 01:13:07.330
Why, that's ridiculous.

01:13:07.330 --> 01:13:08.950
Why, ridiculous?

01:13:08.950 --> 01:13:10.520
Well, you're clothes.

01:13:10.520 --> 01:13:13.320
And you're a foreign accent.

01:13:13.320 --> 01:13:15.010
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha.

01:13:15.010 --> 01:13:17.400
Uh, this is a friend of yours.

01:13:17.400 --> 01:13:19.810
Is she nice?

01:13:19.810 --> 01:13:21.640
Oh, she's rather nice.

01:13:21.640 --> 01:13:25.060
But not nearly so charming as you are.

01:13:25.060 --> 01:13:26.240
Merci.

01:13:26.240 --> 01:13:30.000
You know, you're exactly what I would want to have made of her.

01:13:30.830 --> 01:13:32.910
You don't like her as she is?

01:13:32.910 --> 01:13:34.830
Yes, I do.

01:13:34.830 --> 01:13:38.520
But then she hasn't had the education you have,

01:13:38.520 --> 01:13:40.520
nor the experiences in life.

01:13:40.520 --> 01:13:41.410
No?

01:13:41.410 --> 01:13:42.410
No.

01:13:42.410 --> 01:13:45.330
No, of course not.

01:13:45.330 --> 01:13:47.160
And though she looks like you,

01:13:47.160 --> 01:13:50.720
she isn't nearly as pretty.

01:13:50.720 --> 01:13:52.720
You don't think it might be?

01:13:52.720 --> 01:13:55.120
Well, just the clothes?

01:13:55.120 --> 01:13:56.360
Certainly not.

01:13:56.360 --> 01:13:59.540
Why, clothes mean nothing to me.

01:14:00.000 --> 01:14:04.160
If you were wearing rags, you'd look even more charming.

01:14:04.160 --> 01:14:06.680
Ah, you don't mean that.

01:14:06.680 --> 01:14:08.620
Yes, I do.

01:14:08.620 --> 01:14:11.610
I never believed in love at first sight before.

01:14:11.610 --> 01:14:14.030
But then, it isn't first sight,

01:14:14.030 --> 01:14:16.330
because you're exactly like an elder sister

01:14:16.330 --> 01:14:21.030
of this poor little girl whom I was half in love with already.

01:14:21.030 --> 01:14:22.600
Half in love?

01:14:22.600 --> 01:14:25.590
Well, something like that.

01:14:25.590 --> 01:14:26.710
Nonsense.

01:14:26.710 --> 01:14:27.710
That's not love.

01:14:27.710 --> 01:14:30.000
It's just the effect of this beautiful garden,

01:14:30.030 --> 01:14:31.630
music and and...

01:14:31.630 --> 01:14:33.370
Volsma, Mr. Volsma.

01:14:33.370 --> 01:14:35.370
Ha ha ha, Sally.

01:14:53.060 --> 01:14:57.210
- Big film. - The jet of the Minion.

01:14:57.210 --> 01:14:59.800
- Who? - The jet of the Minion.

01:15:00.190 --> 01:15:01.750
And the prisoner ate a hearty breakfast.

01:15:02.950 --> 01:15:29.060
Your Highness, you remember Madame Noxcarova?

01:15:30.000 --> 01:15:32.000
What name did you say?

01:15:32.000 --> 01:15:34.620
Madame Noscarova.

01:15:34.620 --> 01:15:37.210
Noscarova?

01:15:37.210 --> 01:15:44.170
Why, to be sure, Madame Noscarova.

01:15:44.170 --> 01:15:47.090
Oui, your face is rather familiar.

01:15:47.090 --> 01:15:49.090
You bet your sweet life it is.

01:15:49.090 --> 01:15:52.770
This is indeed a surprise, Madame.

01:15:52.770 --> 01:15:57.640
I'm sure our hostess will pardon us if two old friends take a stroll through the garden.

01:15:57.640 --> 01:16:00.000
Certainly, Your Highness.

01:16:00.350 --> 01:16:02.520
Madam.

01:16:02.520 --> 01:16:13.960
How do you do, Mrs. Tenney?

01:16:13.960 --> 01:16:15.970
Lea, there's a place you weren't coming.

01:16:15.970 --> 01:16:17.970
I'm very sorry, forgive me. Hello, Marcia.

01:16:17.970 --> 01:16:19.830
Who is that beautiful creature?

01:16:19.830 --> 01:16:21.830
Madame Natskorova.

01:16:21.830 --> 01:16:23.680
Are you sure? Positive.

01:16:23.680 --> 01:16:26.370
Oh, she's gorgeous.

01:16:26.370 --> 01:16:30.000
Excuse me, please.

01:16:30.000 --> 01:16:31.850
- What do you make of that?

01:16:31.850 --> 01:16:34.060
- I'm sure I don't know, Mother.

01:16:34.060 --> 01:16:36.220
- Well, I'll soon find out.

01:16:47.770 --> 01:16:49.890
- Sally, what's the game?

01:16:49.890 --> 01:16:51.290
What are you doing here?

01:16:51.290 --> 01:16:53.470
- I, I, well, never mind about that.

01:16:53.470 --> 01:16:54.610
What are you doing here?

01:16:54.610 --> 01:16:55.870
- Well, I-- - Hello, Sally.

01:16:55.870 --> 01:16:56.710
Hello, Connie.

01:16:57.790 --> 01:16:59.040
Oh, don't be frightened.

01:16:59.040 --> 01:17:00.000
I won't give you away.

01:17:00.640 --> 01:17:02.680
but I would like to speak to Sally alone.

01:17:03.710 --> 01:17:04.650
I get you.

01:17:04.840 --> 01:17:08.200
Well, Mulligatone.

01:17:08.200 --> 01:17:12.710
Sally, darling, I haven't thought of anything but you.

01:17:12.710 --> 01:17:15.260
You didn't seem to think so well of me a while ago.

01:17:15.260 --> 01:17:16.880
Oh, I was only kidding.

01:17:16.880 --> 01:17:18.400
I knew who you were all the time.

01:17:18.400 --> 01:17:20.300
- Did you really? - Why, of course.

01:17:20.300 --> 01:17:23.020
Then you're not infatuated with this terrible Noscarova woman.

01:17:23.020 --> 01:17:24.350
Why, no.

01:17:24.350 --> 01:17:28.320
Oh, why didn't you come back to see me last night?

01:17:28.320 --> 01:17:30.000
Why, I told Connie to tell you that I had to

01:17:30.090 --> 01:17:35.080
early to meet some friends at the theater. Oh, I'm so glad. Oh, Sally, you look beautiful.

01:17:35.080 --> 01:17:42.860
Where'd you get this dress? And why Noscarova? Why? Oh, I can't explain now, but you've always

01:17:42.860 --> 01:17:49.500
been so nice to me. You won't give me away, will you? Why, of course not. Oh, Sally, I love you.

01:17:49.500 --> 01:18:00.000
Why, Blam? The matter? Sally, I haven't the right to. They want you for your

01:18:00.000 --> 01:18:00.500
your dance.

01:18:01.280 --> 01:18:02.120
Will you excuse me?

01:18:02.300 --> 01:18:02.640
Certainly.

01:18:04.300 --> 01:18:06.910
You will come back to see me this time, won't you?

01:18:07.010 --> 01:18:07.570
Yes, Sally.

01:18:09.090 --> 01:18:17.720
John, I've just seen the most terrible thing.

01:18:18.080 --> 01:18:18.300
What?

01:18:19.130 --> 01:18:20.830
Blair making love to Nascaruba.

01:18:22.150 --> 01:18:22.550
Nascaruba?

01:18:23.530 --> 01:18:24.430
It's impossible.

01:18:24.870 --> 01:18:26.490
I saw them with my own eyes.

01:18:27.490 --> 01:18:28.750
What's to be done?

01:18:29.290 --> 01:18:30.000
I know.

01:18:30.800 --> 01:18:34.700
I'll announce the engagement of Blair and Marsha immediately after her number.

01:18:35.530 --> 01:18:36.030
All right.

01:18:41.270 --> 01:18:44.290
Ladies and gentlemen, we have a great treat in store for you.

01:18:44.680 --> 01:18:48.990
You are now about to be entertained by none other than the famous Madame Noscarova

01:18:48.990 --> 01:18:50.770
in some of her native dances.

01:20:06.400 --> 01:20:12.800
My dear friends, now that you're all here, it gives me great pleasure to announce the

01:20:12.800 --> 01:20:18.880
engagement of my daughter, Marsha, to Mr. Blair Farrell.

01:20:18.880 --> 01:20:28.040
Now, Madame, you may go on with your dance.

01:20:36.080 --> 01:20:38.010
Don't get it, dirty local.

01:20:38.010 --> 01:20:41.850
Hey, hey, hey, hey, come back here, dirty local.

01:20:41.850 --> 01:20:43.390
- Who's that you now, who's the girl?

01:20:43.390 --> 01:20:44.230
- What girl?

01:20:44.230 --> 01:20:46.390
- You know that girl, my little Sally,

01:20:46.390 --> 01:20:49.100
the one which you stole and kidnapped from my restaurant.

01:20:49.100 --> 01:20:50.480
- I don't know anything about you, Sally.

01:20:50.480 --> 01:20:51.500
- Yes, you do.

01:20:51.500 --> 01:20:52.680
- Hey, listen, if you don't tell us

01:20:52.680 --> 01:20:53.920
what you did to that little girl,

01:20:53.920 --> 01:20:55.340
we're gonna make it bloody tough for you.

01:20:55.340 --> 01:20:57.240
- I tell you, I don't know anything about the girl.

01:20:57.240 --> 01:20:58.240
- You don't!

01:20:58.240 --> 01:21:00.000
- You don't!

01:21:00.830 --> 01:21:03.550
Oh, come on, Luton!

01:21:03.550 --> 01:21:05.550
Listen, where's my sattie?

01:21:05.550 --> 01:21:07.550
Come here! There's my sattie!

01:21:07.550 --> 01:21:09.550
Come on, Luton!

01:21:09.550 --> 01:21:11.550
Don't be stepping on my feet!

01:21:11.550 --> 01:21:13.550
No stepping on your feet!

01:21:13.550 --> 01:21:15.550
Come on, Luton!

01:21:15.550 --> 01:21:18.590
I'll find my sattie!

01:21:20.570 --> 01:21:22.460
There she is!

01:21:22.460 --> 01:21:25.060
There's my sattie!

01:21:25.060 --> 01:21:27.060
Come on, Luton!

01:21:27.060 --> 01:21:30.000
There she is! There's my sattie!

01:21:31.500 --> 01:21:35.270
Oh Sally, I've hunted all over New York for you.

01:21:35.270 --> 01:21:36.470
What does this mean?

01:21:36.470 --> 01:21:39.670
It means the scoundrel here stole my little Sally.

01:21:39.670 --> 01:21:41.870
You, you kid snapper.

01:21:41.870 --> 01:21:43.520
There must be some mistake.

01:21:43.520 --> 01:21:47.080
This is Madame Noscarova, the great Russian dancer.

01:21:47.080 --> 01:21:48.430
You think I'm crazy?

01:21:48.430 --> 01:21:49.930
That's my little Sally.

01:21:49.930 --> 01:21:51.330
Send off, your highness.

01:21:51.330 --> 01:21:52.760
Have you lost your mind?

01:21:52.760 --> 01:21:54.940
This is Madame Noscarova.

01:21:54.940 --> 01:21:57.140
Oh, you leave her my poor head.

01:21:57.140 --> 01:21:58.140
What the heck?

01:21:58.140 --> 01:21:59.670
What's going on here?

01:22:00.000 --> 01:22:01.880
Why, you're drunk. I'm not drunk.

01:22:02.290 --> 01:22:03.630
And I won't be insulted by you.

01:22:04.050 --> 01:22:06.510
You're nobody. Just one of my waiters.

01:22:06.730 --> 01:22:07.210
Waiters?

01:22:07.560 --> 01:22:08.040
Waiters?

01:22:08.300 --> 01:22:08.840
Yes, sir.

01:22:09.180 --> 01:22:10.240
And a rotten waiter.

01:22:10.620 --> 01:22:12.620
Now we know he's mad. Take him away.

01:22:13.010 --> 01:22:14.310
Release Mr. Hooper at once.

01:22:14.330 --> 01:22:15.150
What do you mean, take him back?

01:22:15.270 --> 01:22:18.690
Madam Noscarova, I'm extremely sorry for this, Mr. Serpent.

01:22:19.060 --> 01:22:21.000
Won't you please go on with your dance?

01:22:21.240 --> 01:22:23.520
No. I'm not going to pretend anymore.

01:22:23.780 --> 01:22:24.980
Madam Noscarova.

01:22:24.980 --> 01:22:27.720
Oh, the Duke is just trying to save me from being humiliated.

01:22:28.170 --> 01:22:30.000
He knows I'm not really.

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:31.000
What?

01:22:31.000 --> 01:22:33.160
Mr. Shendorf was right.

01:22:33.160 --> 01:22:36.350
I am Sally, and I work in his restaurant.

01:22:36.350 --> 01:22:39.560
Now that you know this, you want me to dance for you, I will.

01:22:39.560 --> 01:22:40.990
Thank you.

01:22:40.990 --> 01:22:42.990
I don't think we'd be interested in your performance.

01:22:42.990 --> 01:22:44.200
Oh, I see.

01:22:44.200 --> 01:22:48.520
As long as you thought I was this terrible person, you were crazy about me.

01:22:48.520 --> 01:22:50.630
But now you're not interested in me anymore.

01:22:50.630 --> 01:22:52.630
I'm not good enough for you and your guests.

01:22:52.630 --> 01:22:56.020
Mr. Hooper's car for this young lady?

01:22:56.020 --> 01:22:56.990
That won't be necessary.

01:22:56.990 --> 01:23:00.000
Sally, I'll take you home.

01:23:00.760 --> 01:23:04.540
Ladies and gentlemen, we have the honor to bid you goodnight.

01:23:06.600 --> 01:23:07.880
But I can explain all this.

01:23:12.590 --> 01:23:15.550
Sally, I'm terribly sorry about all this.

01:23:16.270 --> 01:23:17.610
You were engaged all the time.

01:23:17.880 --> 01:23:19.600
Oh, Sally, won't you let me explain?

01:23:20.010 --> 01:23:22.410
I don't see how anything could explain that.

01:23:23.530 --> 01:23:24.270
Are you ready, Connie?

01:24:16.220 --> 01:24:18.800
Come in.

01:24:18.800 --> 01:24:20.010
Sally.

01:24:20.010 --> 01:24:21.010
How are you?

01:24:21.010 --> 01:24:22.010
Hello, Sally.

01:24:22.010 --> 01:24:23.010
I'm healthy.

01:24:23.010 --> 01:24:28.280
How do you feel, Sally?

01:24:28.280 --> 01:24:29.590
I'm alright.

01:24:29.590 --> 01:24:30.000
Alright?

01:24:30.320 --> 01:24:34.570
Listen, just cast a fond, loving eye on that, honey.

01:24:36.040 --> 01:24:36.540
What is it?

01:24:36.740 --> 01:24:37.260
What is it?

01:24:39.060 --> 01:24:41.770
Why, it's a contract to feature you in the Ziegfeld Follies.

01:24:46.100 --> 01:24:54.350
What? What's the matter, Sally?

01:24:54.740 --> 01:24:57.480
Come on, come on, snap out of it.

01:24:58.970 --> 01:25:00.000
I wish I could snap out.

01:25:00.000 --> 01:25:03.320
I can't.

01:25:03.440 --> 01:25:04.080
You can't?

01:25:04.580 --> 01:25:06.430
Listen, you know what this means?

01:25:06.770 --> 01:25:08.590
This is an opportunity of a lifetime.

01:25:09.480 --> 01:25:11.540
Why you'll be the biggest hit on Broadway.

01:25:12.470 --> 01:25:14.180
You think so, Otis?

01:25:14.470 --> 01:25:16.150
Do I think so?

01:25:16.450 --> 01:25:17.350
I know it.

01:25:18.040 --> 01:25:20.520
This fellow Ziggy is just crazy about you.

01:25:20.840 --> 01:25:21.280
Really?

01:25:21.660 --> 01:25:22.180
Yes.

01:25:23.270 --> 01:25:24.110
Now what do you say?

01:25:24.370 --> 01:25:24.590
Say?

01:25:24.830 --> 01:25:26.060
Oh, I...

01:25:26.060 --> 01:25:26.620
I...

01:25:26.620 --> 01:25:27.840
Oh, come on now.

01:25:27.920 --> 01:25:28.680
Come on, Sally.

01:25:28.960 --> 01:25:29.160
I do.

01:25:30.990 --> 01:25:35.750
You and Rosie have been so kind to me that I'll try off me hard.

01:25:35.830 --> 01:25:36.730
Oh, that's great.

01:25:36.830 --> 01:25:38.390
Everything is Rosie now, isn't it, Rosie?

01:25:38.770 --> 01:25:39.150
Now listen.

01:26:30.190 --> 01:26:30.870
THE END

01:28:00.410 --> 01:28:00.930
¶¶

01:30:30.700 --> 01:30:31.260
Thank you.

01:32:51.600 --> 01:32:52.220
are red

01:32:52.220 --> 01:32:53.920
and violet blue

01:32:53.920 --> 01:32:55.190
ah

01:32:55.190 --> 01:32:56.240
of course

01:32:56.240 --> 01:32:56.780
that's what it

01:32:56.780 --> 01:32:57.500
gets 20 years

01:32:57.500 --> 01:32:57.940
but that's

01:33:06.750 --> 01:33:14.560
A quaint old Irish sentiment, Mazel Tov, Joseph Ginsberg, ha ha, commercialism.

01:33:16.260 --> 01:33:17.740
What are you doing?

01:33:18.000 --> 01:33:22.170
Oh, I was just putting my card in some of these flowers.

01:33:22.910 --> 01:33:24.730
Well, you've got your nerves.

01:33:25.970 --> 01:33:28.920
Chee-hole, Sally Green!

01:33:36.330 --> 01:33:53.040
Dolly, you're marvelous! I'm proud of you, little girl!

01:33:53.040 --> 01:34:00.000
Surprise! Can I come in?

01:34:00.060 --> 01:34:06.540
the wonderful flowers. Ha! All yours, Sally? I suppose so. Oh, Sally, you were marvelous

01:34:06.540 --> 01:34:13.230
tonight. Gosh, I'm proud to know you. You're the biggest success in New York. Oh, thanks, Connie.

01:34:17.240 --> 01:34:24.960
It doesn't speak to much truth. What? Oh, I know I shouldn't talk to Reagan. Good old friend.

01:34:27.140 --> 01:34:30.000
But that's the way I feel about it.

01:34:33.320 --> 01:34:48.940
I think I understand.

01:34:51.420 --> 01:34:57.200
I get out and give Sally a chance to change her clothes.

01:35:25.720 --> 01:35:26.820
Well, here I am.

01:35:30.000 --> 01:35:32.220
- Hello, Mr. Shendorf.

01:35:32.220 --> 01:35:38.220
- Why, why, sorry, you seem disappointed.

01:35:38.220 --> 01:35:44.630
Was you expecting, Mr. Farrell?

01:35:44.630 --> 01:35:49.960
- See, Leia wrote me two letters asking me to forgive him.

01:35:49.960 --> 01:35:54.920
But I wrote back that I never wanted to speak to him again.

01:35:54.920 --> 01:35:58.480
I haven't heard a thing from him since.

01:35:58.480 --> 01:35:59.800
We haven't felt stilted.

01:36:01.600 --> 01:36:04.920
You know, Sally, I'm the happiest man in the whole world tonight.

01:36:05.430 --> 01:36:08.860
And all because you have made such a wonderful success.

01:36:09.310 --> 01:36:11.920
But I knew you could do it all the time.

01:36:12.220 --> 01:36:13.060
You bet your life.

01:36:13.760 --> 01:36:15.580
Look, look what I've got for you.

01:36:17.160 --> 01:36:19.060
Oh, thank you, Mr. Shandor.

01:36:19.840 --> 01:36:21.220
They didn't come for me.

01:36:22.060 --> 01:36:22.380
No?

01:36:22.660 --> 01:36:23.200
No, no.

01:36:23.200 --> 01:36:25.760
Here, look inside at the note where it says.

01:36:30.960 --> 01:36:34.270
He says he's awfully sorry for what happened to me on that night.

01:36:35.700 --> 01:36:41.230
Someday, when I forgive him, if I ever do, I'm to send him one of these roses.

01:36:42.730 --> 01:36:43.890
Well, how are you going to keep them?

01:36:44.780 --> 01:36:48.120
You know, after two or three days, you know, they won't smell so pretty.

01:36:49.010 --> 01:36:56.700
You, uh, want me to, uh, give it to him now?

01:36:58.780 --> 01:37:00.000
Mm-hmm.

01:37:01.880 --> 01:37:02.980
If you can find him.

01:37:08.430 --> 01:37:09.590
Well, I'll find him.

01:37:10.130 --> 01:37:16.710
You know, it may take a week, or it might take a month, but I'll find him.

01:37:22.410 --> 01:37:22.930
Oh, Sally?

01:37:23.660 --> 01:37:24.380
Yeah?

01:37:24.810 --> 01:37:26.550
Suppose I find Mr. Farrell.

01:37:27.630 --> 01:37:30.000
Should I tell him that you forgive him?

01:37:30.000 --> 01:37:35.930
Yes. But don't do that. I want to make him ask me a lot of times before I forgive him.

01:37:35.930 --> 01:37:43.700
Oh, I see. You don't want to think he, uh, don't want him to think that you've just been waiting for him to come around, huh?

01:37:43.700 --> 01:37:44.660
That's it, exactly.

01:37:44.660 --> 01:37:46.660
Uh-huh. I see.

01:37:46.660 --> 01:37:59.190
Agenda! Oh, Agenda!

01:38:02.810 --> 01:38:03.810
